   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "To say that...",
     "texto": [
      "With **сказать** («to say»), **ответить** («to answer») and **написать** («to write») use **что** + clause: **Он сказал, что приедет** («He said he would come»). If the original person said «Я приду», when reporting it you say **Он сказал, что придёт** («He said he would come»): the person changes, not the tense.",
      "To say it to someone, use the dative: **Он сказал мне, что занят** («He told me he is busy»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Past and present",
     "texto": [
      "The verb form depends on the meaning and on the moment from which the story is told: **Она сказала, что вчера была дома** («She said that yesterday she had been at home»); **Он сказал, что сейчас занят** («He said that he is busy now»).",
      "Time expressions are understood from the context. If the «tomorrow» of the quote has already passed, the report can say **Он сказал, что придёт на следующий день** («He said he would come the next day»). There is no automatic change: the intended time relation is kept."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
